course: dictionary
lesson: 1223
title: Describing shapes with bulgy
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words paint a picture in one go, and bulgy is one of them. It means swelling out in round lumps, like something pushing out at the sides. «Long ago elephants had no trunk, only a bulgy nose as big as a boot.» You can almost see that nose: round, puffed out and lumpy.
explain: Context helps you check the meaning. The nose was as big as a boot, so it was large and round, not flat or thin. A bulgy bag is one stuffed so full that its sides push out. Swap in bulging: «a bulging nose as big as a boot» still makes sense, so bulgy means bulging.
explain: Bulgy is informal and a bit funny, so writers use it in stories and everyday talk rather than in formal reports. A monster with bulgy eyes sounds playful and silly, which is why an author might choose it.
fact: Bulgy means swelling out in round lumps, or bulging.
fact: «A bulgy nose as big as a boot» describes a nose that is large and round.
fact: A bulgy bag is one stuffed so full that its sides push out.
fact: Bulgy is informal and a bit funny, so it suits stories and talk more than formal writing.
fact: Bulgier and bulgiest show more: a bulgier bag is fuller, and the bulgiest is the fullest of all.
exercise: «Long ago elephants had no trunk, only a bulgy nose as big as a boot.» What does bulgy mean? | Long and thin like a stick | *Swelling out in round lumps | Very quiet and still | Shiny and smooth
exercise: Which bag is bulgy? | A thin, pointed pencil | *A shopping bag stuffed so full it pushes out at the sides | A flat, empty envelope | A tiny button on a coat
exercise: Which word could replace bulgy in «a bulgy nose» without changing the meaning? | bendy | brief | *bulging | bright
test: «The monster had bulgy eyes that stared out of its head.» What does bulgy suggest about the eyes? | They are hidden under a hat | They are tiny and dark | *They stick out in round lumps | They are closed tightly
test: Why is bulgy a fun word to use in a story? | *It is informal and a bit funny, so it adds a playful, vivid shape | It only describes sounds | It means the same as thin | It is a formal word for a report
exam: Which sentence uses bulgy correctly? | He wrote a bulgy report for the head teacher | *Her coat was bulgy with conkers stuffed in every pocket | The sky was bulgy and blue | She sang a bulgy song at assembly
